    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I am interested in creating a base16 colorscheme that use's my works branding colors as the base. It would be really nice if there was a way to live update a buffer with the changed theme without having to quit and reopen nvim.\r\n\r\nHas anyone accomplished this before?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am interested in creating a base16 colorscheme that use's my works branding colors as the base. It would be really nice if there was a way to live update a buffer with the changed theme without having to quit and reopen nvim.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Has anyone accomplished this before?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I am interested in creating a base16 colorscheme that use's my works branding colors as the base. It would be really nice if there was a way to live update a buffer with the changed theme without having to quit and reopen nvim.\nHas anyone accomplished this before?",
