            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It's a bit complex, but take a look at the [new dev mode in 'folke/tokyonightnvim](https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim/blob/main/.lazy.lua). It would need adjustments, though, depending on how you organize color scheme files.\n\nAlso it utilizes 'mini.hipatterns' from 'mini.nvim', so you should be half way there :)",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It's a bit complex, but take a look at the <a href=\"https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim/blob/main/.lazy.lua\">new dev mode in 'folke/tokyonightnvim</a>. It would need adjustments, though, depending on how you organize color scheme files.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also it utilizes 'mini.hipatterns' from 'mini.nvim', so you should be half way there :)</p>",
            "bodyText": "It's a bit complex, but take a look at the new dev mode in 'folke/tokyonightnvim. It would need adjustments, though, depending on how you organize color scheme files.\nAlso it utilizes 'mini.hipatterns' from 'mini.nvim', so you should be half way there :)",
